# PROJECT: SMART HOSTEL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
## Full-Stack Web Application — Landing Page, Authentication, and Role-Based Dashboard

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, product designer, UX architect, and database engineer. Build a complete, functional, responsive Hostel Management System with a professional, production-oriented interface.

The project must include a public landing page, login page, student registration page, protected dashboards, and the essential hostel management modules described below.

Do not build just a static UI mockup. Implement working navigation, forms, validation, authentication, CRUD operations, database integration, filtering, status updates, and role-based access control.

Use the two supplied reference images as follows:

- **Reference Image 1:** Source of the Hostel Management System requirements, user roles, workflows, and feature modules.
- **Reference Image 2:** The primary visual design reference. Follow its neutral grey surfaces, dark navy accents, compact navigation sidebar, white content panels, restrained borders, and clean data-dense dashboard layout.

The result should look like a professionally designed product built by a real software team, not a generic AI-generated website.

---

# 1. PRODUCT IDENTITY

Product name: HostelEase

Product category: Hostel Administration and Student Welfare Management Platform.

Tagline: "Better hostel management. A better student experience."

Purpose:
Create one centralized digital platform to manage hostel residents, room allocations, attendance, fee payments, leave requests, complaints, visitors, mess menus, maintenance, notices, and administrative reports.

Primary users:
1. Hostel Administrator / Warden
2. Student / Hostel Resident
3. Hostel Staff

Build a coherent system where all three roles use the same application but see different interfaces and permissions.

Do not create three unrelated websites. Use a shared design system, authentication system, database, and application architecture.

